## Key Predictors (Odds Ratios)

| Variable | OR | Interpretation |
|----------|----|----------------|
| Child age (months) | 1.104 | Higher odds of stunting with increasing age |
| BMI | 0.992 | Protective association |
| Not breastfed (BD2No) | 1.171 | Higher odds of stunting |
| Wealth index (Richest) | 0.366 | Strong protective effect |
| Maternal education (Higher) | 0.439 | Protective effect |

---

## Interpretation of Results

- Older children were associated with higher odds of stunting.
- Children who were not breastfed (BD2No) had higher odds of stunting.
- Higher maternal BMI showed a protective association against stunting.
- Household wealth showed a strong protective gradient, with richer households having lower odds of stunting.
- Higher maternal education was associated with reduced odds of stunting.
- Child sex was not a statistically significant predictor in this model.

